1
00:00:00,088 --> 00:00:05,388
We built AI Radar because finding a paper and understanding it are
two different

2
00:00:05,388 --> 00:00:06,088
challenges.

3
00:00:06,475 --> 00:00:11,562
Researchers need to keep up, while students entering a new field
can feel lost

4
00:00:11,562 --> 00:00:12,575
in technical language.

5
00:00:12,988 --> 00:00:14,775
We wanted to make that first step easier.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,938
The homepage keeps things simple: a central search box, saved
category shortcuts,

7
00:00:21,162 --> 00:00:22,838
and monthly submission rankings.

8
00:00:23,225 --> 00:00:26,462
Deep reading and language settings are available at the top.

9
00:00:27,267 --> 00:00:31,029
Search an official arXiv category by name or code.

10
00:00:31,492 --> 00:00:36,454
For example, C S dot A I takes us straight to artificial
intelligence.

11
00:00:37,254 --> 00:00:43,317
Selecting a category retrieves up to five recent papers and
generates an overview.

12
00:00:43,729 --> 00:00:48,329
Here, we're opening a saved report, starting with the shared
research context.

13
00:00:49,142 --> 00:00:53,567
Each paper pairs a plain language explanation with a concrete
illustration.

14
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:57,904
This example shows an agent learning to avoid tools that have
stopped working.

15
00:00:58,671 --> 00:01:03,858
Expand a card to explore the problem, approach, results, and
limitations.

16
00:01:04,258 --> 00:01:08,621
The illustrations explain concepts; they aren't experimental
results.

17
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:12,358
The deep reading button opens a compact paper list.

18
00:01:12,771 --> 00:01:17,546
Choose one paper for individual reading, or several for joint
analysis.

19
00:01:17,946 --> 00:01:20,033
You decide what belongs in the collection.

20
00:01:20,838 --> 00:01:25,988
In the reading workspace, you can upload your own PDFs, replace a
source, or remove

21
00:01:25,988 --> 00:01:26,500
a paper.

22
00:01:26,888 --> 00:01:30,462
Resolve any failed material, then click Generate Report.

23
00:01:31,254 --> 00:01:35,592
Now we're switching to a separate, previously generated English
joint report.

24
00:01:35,992 --> 00:01:40,629
This example brings together two papers covering seventy five
pages.

25
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:46,558
The report connects their research questions and compares methods,
results, and

26
00:01:46,558 --> 00:01:51,633
limitations, while keeping each paper's identity and experimental
context visible.

27
00:01:52,408 --> 00:01:57,683
Click a citation to see the original excerpt, its paper, and its
PDF page.

28
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:02,833
Automated checks help trace the evidence, but important scientific
claims still

29
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:03,708
need your judgment.

30
00:02:04,517 --> 00:02:07,029
The interface supports English and Chinese.

31
00:02:07,442 --> 00:02:12,792
Reports can be English, Chinese, or bilingual, with interface and
report languages

32
00:02:12,792 --> 00:02:13,942
selected independently.

33
00:02:14,754 --> 00:02:19,867
Our biggest lesson was turning a vague idea into clear
requirements, then breaking

34
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:22,517
a large feature into manageable tasks.

35
00:02:22,904 --> 00:02:26,592
We learned through planning, building, testing, and feedback.

36
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:33,004
We believe AI Radar deserves recognition because it connects
discovery, understandable

37
00:02:33,017 --> 00:02:38,717
explanations, and traceable evidence in one workflow, helping
people approach unfamiliar

38
00:02:38,729 --> 00:02:40,454
research with greater confidence.

39
00:02:41,267 --> 00:02:46,029
With user validation, this could grow into a product with saved
libraries, topic

40
00:02:46,029 --> 00:02:48,354
updates, and shared team workspaces.

41
00:02:48,767 --> 00:02:53,404
A free discovery tier and paid reading tools are possibilities to
explore.

42
00:02:53,817 --> 00:02:57,067
Our goal is to turn more papers into useful knowledge.
